turnkey-apache-php-19.0 (1) turnkey; urgency=low

  * Initial release of the Apache and PHP stack layer for Keel, compatible
    with TurnKey Linux appliances. Built as a layer on core:
    bt-layer apache-php --parent core.

  * What LAMP and LAPP have in common, built once: Apache 2 with mod_php,
    php-cli, mod_security2, mod_evasive, mod_perl2, the Webmin modules for
    Apache and for php.ini, Adminer with the syntax highlighter it
    recommends, Composer, and the web control panel assets. From the shared
    tree: the apache, php, adminer, composer and tkl-webcp overlays, and the
    conf scripts apache-vhost, apache-headers, apache-security, apache-ssl,
    php, adminer, adminer-apache, apache-cgi and tkl-webcp.

  * The default site serves /var/www on 80 and on 443, which is what both
    upstream recipes replace Debian's default with. mod_cgi is enabled and
    serve-cgi-bin.conf points at /var/www/cgi-bin.

  * Decision 0013 is why this layer can exist: a database is a component
    carried by a fab unit, not a parent layer, so LAMP is this layer plus the
    mariadb unit and LAPP is this layer plus the postgresql unit. Before
    that, each stack had to be a child of its own database and the web half
    was built twice.

  * What is deliberately not here, because it belongs to one stack and not to
    both: the database and its unit, the Adminer configuration that names one
    (conf/adminer-mysql, conf/adminer-pgsql), the confconsole overlay per
    stack, the landing page, and each stack's own extras (php-xdebug,
    php-pear and the Python and Perl database drivers).

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
